Migration Strategy
Problem
The platform's non-custodial compute integration was not properly functioning, with several key issues:

Broken inference workflow: Chat requests with NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_NONCUSTODIAL_INFERENCE=true were not reaching the 0G providers correctly
Missing logging chain: The expected [CHAT] and [PROXY] log markers were not appearing for debugging
UI contrast problems: The "back to agents" button in /agent/[id]/chat had white background making text invisible
Incomplete ledger integration: LedgerBalance component was not properly integrated into chat interfaces
Poor error handling: Storage retrieve API lacked graceful fallbacks for missing metadata files
Solution
Non-custodial Inference Pipeline
Enhanced the complete workflow using the 0G SDK pattern from 0g-serving-user-broker:

// Before: Basic proxy without proper preparation
const response = await fetch('/api/compute/chat', { ... })

// After: Full prepare → proxy → processResponse workflow  
const preparedRequest = await prepareComputeRequest(providerAddress, payload)
const result = await broker.inference.processResponse(providerAddress, content, chatId)
The chat API now properly detects non-custodial mode and forwards prepared requests to the proxy endpoint with comprehensive logging:

console.log('[CHAT] start - Beginning non-custodial chat request')
console.log('[CHAT] prepared - Checking wallet availability...')  
console.log('[CHAT] fetch - Sending to chat API...')
console.log('[CHAT] HIT - Request prepared successfully')
console.log('[PROXY] HIT - Forwarding to proxy endpoint')
Ledger Account Management
Integrated the existing LedgerBalance component into chat interfaces with auto-creation functionality:

Desktop: Compact ledger display in chat header
Mobile: Full ledger component above chat
Auto-creation: Separate ledger per wallet with 0.01 ETH initial balance
Top-up buttons: Quick 0.01, 0.05, 0.1 ETH options
UI Accessibility Improvements
Fixed contrast issues throughout the interface:

// Before: Invisible white-on-white button
className="border-white/20 text-white hover:bg-white/10"

// After: Transparent with proper contrast  
className="bg-transparent/0 hover:bg-white/10 border border-white/20 hover:border-white/40 text-white"
Enhanced button and badge variants with gradient backgrounds instead of low-contrast outline styles.

Error Handling & Storage
Added graceful error handling in /api/storage/retrieve with specific ENOENT detection:

} catch (fileError: any) {
  if (fileError.code === 'ENOENT') {
    console.log('[Storage Retrieve] ENOENT - File does not exist, will use fallback')
  }
  // Graceful fallback to generated metadata
}
